                <pb facs="1008" n="892" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg892"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.2311/34.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Governor of Texas to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Austin, Texas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 10, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram [of February 9] received. Am advised that railroad communication
                    between Juárez and Chihuahua is open, but south of Chihuahua the railroad is in
                    hands of revolting party.</p>
                <p>If Mexican troops pass through Texas from Eagle Pass to Juárez, is there any
                    assurance that they will not be met with armed resistance in attempting to enter
                    Juárez from Texas?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">O. B. Colquitt.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
